 "_comment": "One secret-pattern source for Python has_secret and Node containsSecret. Held: a known token shape, a Luhn-valid card, or a password/key keyword followed by a literal value (the value has a digit or symbol and is not a placeholder or a call). Not held: an identifier, attribute, call, '...', a 'moved to' note, or a placeholder; 'placeholder' is the one shared list, {PH} in a rule. Both sides run these ASCII-only on normalized text (NFKC, casefold, whitespace/control to space, non-ASCII letter to x, digit to 0). Cards: 16 digits (Luhn) standing alone; a later 16-digit window in a grouped run also needs a card-network prefix (card_iin) and 1-4 groups before, at most 4 after, at most 2 of 4+ digits per side; 'amex' is 15 digits starting 34/37; a card that is on the published test_cards list (the fake numbers payment processors document; no real account) is not a secret; a whole USPS 'tracking' run with a valid check digit is removed before the card check.",
